# .trivyignore — Trivy vulnerability suppressions for runtime image scans.
#
# Both entries are HIGH findings in the LangChain/LangGraph application stack
# whose fixed versions require a coordinated major-version migration
# (langchain-core 0.3.x -> 1.x together with langgraph >= 0.7 and the
# langgraph-sdk 0.4.x line). The runtime pins langchain-core to <0.4 in
# services/agent-runtime/pyproject.toml and services/rag-runtime/pyproject.toml;
# moving past that is a tracked migration, not a point fix. The scan still
# reports every other finding, including any new HIGH/CRITICAL introduced later.
#
# Review / remediate by: 2026-12-31
#   - CVE-2026-34070: langchain-core path traversal in legacy load_prompt
#     functions; fixed in 1.2.22. Requires the langchain-core 1.x migration.
#   - CVE-2026-104873: langgraph-sdk authorization bypass; fixed in 0.4.4.
#     Requires bumping langgraph to a release that accepts langgraph-sdk 0.4.x.

CVE-2026-34070
CVE-2026-104873
